CI facts are a Postgres row, never model text (ADR 0018, ADR 0035). `check_run` and `status` deliveries call `applyPrHeadCiFact` in the same `inTransaction` as `insertWebhookEvent` and enqueue `CI_PROJECTION_QUEUE` through `requestHeadCiProjection`, the only enqueue path; `classifySnapshot` derives the rollup, and an incomplete check page is `unknown`, not passing. The model fills only `headline`, `reason`, `fixHint` (`ciSummaryLlmSchema`); `mergeCiSummaryWithFacts` overwrites `status` and failure names from facts, and `authorHeadCiIfFactsChanged` runs one turn per `hashCiFacts` change. Ack, ticks, and publish render the cell from the row and stamp `v=<version>`. Later writes use only `applyCiProjectionBodyUpdate`: `head` must match unless superseded, `v` must be older; the verification-failure block is re-injected. `reviewVerdict.ts` is the single writer for the `PR Agent Review` check and `pr-agent/review` status. Three modules own the code: `ciFacts.ts` (snapshot types, `classifyS
